A||||1||batboy||PISA's Big Fiero Book
Z||000000||batboy||08-02-99||08:54 PM||||I am considering buying that PISA Corp's "Big Fiero Book". Does anybody out there have it? If so, is it worth the $20? What other Fiero books should I consider for my library?
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-03-99||07:51 AM||||I bought PISA's Big Fiero Parts Book and I think it was worth it.  It's by no means comprehensive, but it does list about 20 Fiero parts vendors with details on what they offer.<p>Mark Corbin's Fiero Spotters Guide ($5) and Brooklands Pontiac Fiero: 1984-1988 ($20) are also great.  My favorite Fiero book is Gary Witzenberg's Fiero - hardcover with glossy color pages.  Lots of great photos and info.  It's out of print and the Fiero Store is asking something like $35 for it, but I think it's worth it.
